-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the ground state of the electric field for given charges
-- The electric part of the Hamiltonian is diagonal in the charge-network basis, so for fixed charges at the
-- vertices and fixed states of the geometry the field's ground state is the label assignment, among those obeying
-- Gauss's law, of least energy. Here every assignment with labels in [−B, B] is weighed, exactly.
sq-range-from : Nat → SQ → List SQ
sq-range-from f x = case f of
  zero → nil
  suc g → cons x (sq-range-from g (sq-plus x sq-one))
